// Title: Access to Browser Login Data
// ID: fc028194-969d-4122-8abe-0470d5b8f12f
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-01-30
// Tags: attack.credential-access, attack.t1555.003
// Description: Adversaries may acquire credentials from web browsers by reading files specific to the target browser.
// Web browsers commonly save credentials such as website usernames and passwords so that they do not need to be entered manually in the future.
// Web browsers typically store the credentials in an encrypted format within a credential store.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

any where (((ScriptBlockText like "*_Copy-Item*" and ScriptBlockText like "*_-Destination*")) and ((ScriptBlockText like "*_\\Opera Software\\Opera Stable\\Login Data*" or ScriptBlockText like "*_\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Profiles*" or ScriptBlockText like "*_\\Microsoft\\Edge\\User Data\\Default*" or ScriptBlockText like "*_\\Google\\Chrome\\User Data\\Default\\Login Data*" or ScriptBlockText like "*_\\Google\\Chrome\\User Data\\Default\\Login Data For Account*")))
